    <h1 class="page-title">Tejas Mahajan</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am a PhD student in Computer Science at the
        <a href="https://www.ucf.edu/">University of Central Florida</a>, working in the
        <a href="https://www.cs.ucf.edu/compbio/">Computational Biology Lab</a>
        with Dr. Wei Zhang as a Graduate Research Assistant. I also serve as a Teaching Assistant
        in the Department of Computer Science. My expected graduation is 2031. I am based in Orlando, Florida.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work focuses on single-cell multi-omics, machine learning, AI security, and quantitative
        methods, with an emphasis on computer science and systems fundamentals. Alongside research,
        I build research tools and systems software in Python, C++, and Rust.
      </p>
      <p>
        This blog is for technical explanations of things I have built or am studying — how a method
        works, what tradeoffs it makes, and where it still falls short. It is not a publication list.
        For research software, manuscripts, and project demos, see my
        <a href="https://tejas-ml.github.io/">portfolio</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
